  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1230 AM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nModels move the upper trough across the central Rockies and into \nthe Plains bringing a cold front through South-Central Texas \nThursday night into Friday. The best combination lift and moisture\nis looking like the Rio Grande region. There will be the \npossibility of locally heavy rain out there Thursday night/Friday.\nRain chances have decreased over the eastern half of the area, \nand it is now looking like a dry forecast. Behind the front \ntemperatures will be lower Friday through Sunday. Low temperatures\nnext weekend could be in the 50s and highs in the 70s for most of\nthe area. The low level flow will switch back around to the \nsoutheast by next Monday starting another warming trend.",
